comments:
As far as CIDR inclusion goes, I think that, at least for ingest purposes, supporting something similar to the functionality of the `contains` method from [netty](https://netty.io/3.5/api/org/jboss/netty/handler/ipfilter/CIDR.html) would be sufficient.

So, in the case of doing an ip address check for inclusion in a CIDR blocks. Something to the effect of:

```
def block = new CIDR("192.168.0.0/8");
if (block.contains("192.168.1.1")) {
...
}
```

Alternatively, we could also do something similar to the CIDR matching implementation in EQL. Exposing `CIDRUtils.isInRange` to the execution context seems like it'd be sufficient for most ingest purposes that I can think of:

https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/709068da7cf6e11e3148e67eac211a088affce4a/x-pack/plugin/eql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/eql/expression/function/scalar/string/CIDRUtils.java#L23

